From 0b4360ee832df17cec4978a28ea5aa28b3784d45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:29:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] redfin 1036: GPU DCVS, kern.sweet_gpu_dcvs (default 0 = fixed
 sweetgpufreq level)

The A620 runs at the fixed sweetgpufreq level (r64u: 4 = 625 MHz) whatever the load. kern.sweet_gpu_dcvs 1 starts a
16 ms governor: busy from the GMU XO busy counter (Linux a6xx_hw_init / a6xx_gpu_busy: CX_BUSY_MASK 0xff000000,
POWER_COUNTER_SELECT_0 countable 0x20, XOCLK_0; CP per-submit stamps if it does not count), target ~50 %: up at once
to the level covering 1.1 x need, top after a window > 85 % or 50 ms continuously busy, down one level after 4
quiet windows, floor after 80 ms idle; touch / frames-flowing hints from 0970's sweet_cpufreq_boost hold the top for
kern.sweet_gpu_dcvs_boost_ms (1000). 0964's thermal cap is the ceiling. Votes through the HFI perf vote (msg 30) with a
20 us ack poll. Bits 2/4 drop the touch / SwapEnd boost. kern.sweet_gpu_dcvs_floor MHz (400), kern.sweet_gpu_mhz (read).
Line: SWEET GPU DCVS 5s: 275:ms 400:ms 500:ms 625:ms ms | switches N | busy P% | boosts B capped C | floor F cap T | src gmu|cp.
UniXNU reference: sheng GpuPowerProbe.cpp gpuDcvsThread.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC2ugyLE29nbFLJoQZd
